My experience at Gems International School influenced my technical, interpersonal, and leadership abilities. I took advantage of a variety of chances as a student that sharpened my leadership, teamwork, and innovation skills. I developed a strong feeling of responsibility and collaboration by participating in significant school activities and serving as a student council leader for three consecutive terms.

Through practical projects like a self-balancing robot and a gesture-controlled robotic arm, I also investigated my love for technology, which stoked my interest in the Internet of Things.

Beyond academics, my involvement in exchange programs, global platforms, and competitive arenas broadened my perspective and helped me grow as a well-rounded individual. It was a cornerstone of my development, preparing me to approach the future with confidence.

As all things come to an end, so did my journey at Gems International School. Reflecting on the five years I spent there, I realize how much I’ve grown both personally and professionally. Every experience shaped who I am today. The friendships, the challenges, the moments of success, and even the setbacks all contributed to my growth. My farewell wasn’t just a goodbye to the school, but to a chapter that prepared me for the future with memories, and valuable life lessons.

My football journey at school was a defining part of my leadership and teamwork development. As the captain of the school football team, I led our squad in friendly matches, local competitions, and prestigious events like GIFA by Hindustan Times 2018 and Adidas Uprising 2018, where I was honoured with the Best Player award. Additionally, I played for my local club, Fhamrock Football Academy, and participated in the Delhi Youth League as the team’s left-back.

I had the honor of leading Concordia MUN in 2022 as Head of Media and Design. I was in charge of designing the conference's visual identity and producing all media pieces, including event designs and promotional content. I was able to work independently to make sure the event was a success while honing my creativity, time management, and problem-solving abilities. It made me realize how crucial flexibility and independence are to effective leadership.

Being sworn in as School President during my investiture ceremony was a moment of immense pride. Having served in three consecutive student councils, I gained invaluable leadership experience. In the past, ss the youngest Ruby House Captain, I learned to lead with confidence and resilience. My time as President of the Innovation Club, where we worked with Arduinos on creative projects, further honed my problem-solving skills and reinforced my passion for innovation and leadership.

My 2022 TEDxGEMSInternationalSchool talk on gender stereotypes was a life-changing event. It encouraged me to delve deeper into the cultural conventions that influence how we view gender and provided me with a forum to express my ideas to a wide range of listeners. In addition to improving my public speaking abilities, this event strengthened my desire to promote equality. It was a turning point that gave me the confidence to keep dispelling myths and advocating for inclusiveness.

In 2018, I participated in the 7th Mauritius Society of Quality Control Circles, where I took part in a Case Study Presentation, Dance Competition, and Poster Making Competition. This experience allowed me to showcase creativity and teamwork while exploring the beauty of Mauritius. We visited stunning reefs, the Grand Bassin Temple, Casela Nature Park, and the Parliament. Immersing in local culture made this event a perfect blend of professional growth and unforgettable exploration.

I was one of 15 students chosen for the Dubai Student Exchange Program in 2018, which was an amazing opportunity. I spent two weeks immersed in the dynamic culture of the United Arab Emirates, attending local schools and touring famous sites like Ferrari World, the Grand Mosque, and the Burj Khalifa. From the Miracle Garden to desert safaris, every event created fresh insights and priceless memories. This trip inspired me to value variety, international relationships, and the wonders of travel.

Driven by my passion for design and visual storytelling, I pursued a certification in Digital Film Making at MAAC. This step was fueled by my desire to bring creative ideas to life through professional tools and techniques. The program deepened my understanding of Adobe Photoshop, After Effects, Audition, Premiere Pro, and Media Encoder, sharpening my technical skills and empowering me to express my vision with precision.

I explored the pre-production process, delving into storyboarding and scripting, which enhanced my ability to structure concepts effectively. Learning the basics of cinematography and camera handling added a new dimension to my creativity, allowing me to appreciate the art of composition and framing. This experience didn’t just teach me design—it amplified my love for it, pushing me to think innovatively and refine my craft. My journey at MAAC reaffirmed my commitment to creativity, inspiring me to pursue excellence in visual media.

My journey into technology and personal growth began at RN Podar. Here, I was first introduced to the world of programming and computers, which ignited my passion for technology. I began with Alice, a beginner-friendly programming language, and learned Microsoft PowerPoint, which sparked my interest in software and presentation design. These early experiences laid the groundwork for my deep curiosity and drive to explore everything related to computers. Beyond technology, RN Podar was also where I began to develop key skills in public speaking and leadership, as I explored my passion for football. These formative years were not just about academics but about discovering my diverse interests, including sports and presentations, that would shape my future. RN Podar played a crucial role in shaping my foundation for learning, creativity, and curiosity, helping me realize the power of technology and communication in both personal and professional growth.

During my 3-month internship at Clinigo, a VITTBI company focused on digitizing healthcare, I had the opportunity to work as a Social Media Manager for LinkedIn and Instagram. Clinigo was in its early stages, and the product was not yet available to the market, which made the challenge even more exciting. My role involved collaborating with a talented design team to create engaging content that communicated the company’s vision and raised awareness about digital healthcare solutions.

I was responsible for strategizing and planning social media content, ensuring that it was both informative and appealing to our audience. Working closely with my co-workers, we focused on creating posts that highlighted various healthcare topics. We also worked on blogs, stories, and posts tied to key dates in the healthcare sector, such as World Polio Week, to engage with a broader audience. These posts were aimed at educating the public about healthcare innovation while also sparking meaningful conversations.

Our organic approach yielded impressive results. Through consistent and strategic content, we achieved a remarkable 70% growth in social media engagement. This success was driven by the power of organic reach, effective audience interaction, and timely, relevant content. It was a testament to the strength of word-of-mouth marketing in building brand awareness, especially when the product was still in development.

This experience taught me valuable lessons in social media management, including content planning, audience engagement, and performance analysis. I also developed a deeper understanding of digital healthcare and the importance of effective communication in bringing innovative ideas to life. My time at Clinigo reinforced my passion for technology and its potential to revolutionize industries, especially healthcare. It was a truly rewarding experience that allowed me to apply my skills while contributing to an exciting, forward-thinking company.

