Creya Teacher

GEMS International School Gurgaon · Internship

Apr 2023 - Jul 2023 · 4 mos

Gurugram, Haryana, India · On-site


During my internship at Gems International School as a Creya Instructor, I had the opportunity to contribute to the school’s STEAM Learning program, which focuses on sparking curiosity and hands-on learning in science, technology, engineering, arts, and mathematics. I was tasked with assisting teachers and guiding students from classes 2 to 8, helping them explore fundamental concepts about how machines work and encouraging them to build their own creations. The program offered a unique blend of structured learning and creativity, providing young minds with a solid foundation in engineering principles through hands-on projects.

My role involved introducing students to the basics of breadboards, where they learned how to connect circuits and make simple machines such as motors, levers, and pulleys. These projects not only enhanced their understanding of electrical and mechanical engineering but also encouraged them to think critically and problem-solve in a fun and engaging way. I worked closely with the students to ensure they understood the concepts, guiding them step-by-step through their projects while allowing them the freedom to explore and innovate on their own.

To make learning even more engaging, we incorporated fun and interactive activities such as Lego time, where students could build and experiment with Lego sets to reinforce the principles they were learning. This hands-on approach to learning was aimed at making complex concepts more approachable, and it was incredibly rewarding to see students excited about applying what they learned in real-world scenarios.

This internship was an invaluable experience for me, as it allowed me to pass on the passion and enthusiasm for technology and innovation that I had experienced as a child. It was an opportunity to not only share my knowledge but also inspire young students to discover the world of STEAM for themselves.

